Z||000018||Wes Tausend||01-17-2001||10:51 AM||||RossT,<P>Thank you for the welcome.<P>I'm working on a non-Fiero kit and frequently post with the same moniker on another forum, <A HREF="http://www.cobraforum.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cobraforum.com</A>  . I know what you mean by feeling isolated in our city.<P>I very much admire the clever engineering that went into the Fiero and find it appalling that Pontiac quit just when they got it perfected.  What were they thinking!?<P>My wife is a Corvette fan so we have an ongoing friendly rivalry. You are welcome to check out our cars someday if you wish. I am in the directory.<P>Wes||||reg||1
Z||000019||mshill||01-17-2001||03:53 PM||||RossT, the Euroworks outfit is highly touted by the whole "kitcar" community and especially Kurt Scott.  The more I investigate and the deeper I get into my kit project, the more I realize that a kit is just one step short of a one-off production of a car.  I don't care if it is advertised as a bolt-on rebody, it is going to be more work that you anticipated.  My kit, has great glass work, but lacks in documentation.  Where others like Euroworks touts their documentation but it sounds like it lacked a little in the fibreglass quality area.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Phil||01-17-2001||07:31 PM||||My Lambo kit is also a Euro works and if is definately NOT any way near bolt on. I had to open one rear wheel opening 2" to match the other side and no measurements are the same from one side to the other. But in it's defense it did introduce me to Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Wes Tausend||01-17-2001||08:24 PM||||mshill, Phil,<P>I believe Jason bought the Euroworks body because it was designed to be very close to original appearance. He didn't seem to mind the fabricating to install the body at all in spite of very little documentation but the body was not nearly as straight as it could have been. In his case the body may have been pulled from the mold too soon which encourages sagging and panel warpage. Another factor may be that polyester resin was probably used which does not cure as warp resistant as the newer more expensive vinyl ester resins. It is also difficult for a low production fiberglass kit operation to have the artistic skills that a major boat manufacturer may have so all kit buyers beware. My $.02.<P>Wes||||reg||1
